  {
   "type": "text",
   "title": "",
   "options": {
    "mode": "markdown",
    "content": "### Outage turns into a retry storm\n**Guide:** Failure modes: row 7  \u00b7  **Symptom:** API outage multiplies its own load.  \u00b7  **Cause:** Every workflow retrying in process at short backoffs.  \u00b7  **Fix:** MaximumAttempts cap, circuit breaker, non-retryable errors for client faults.\n\n**What to watch:** API requests/s (503) during each outage window: dozens of times the normal rate when broken, near zero once the breaker opens.\n\n| # | Variant | Phase | Length | What changes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | baseline | normal (2% invalid cards) | 45 s |  |\n| 2 | broken | outage: 250 ms constant retries, no cap | 75 s | Unlimited attempts every 250 ms for 10 s, invalid cards retried too, no per-worker rate cap. |\n| 3 | baseline | recover | 45 s |  |\n| 4 | fixed | outage: capped retries + breaker + fallback | 75 s | 4 attempts with backoff inside 2 s, InvalidRequest non-retryable, breaker fails fast, result 'deferred'. |\n| 5 | baseline | normal | 45 s |  |\n\nRun it from the [control page](http://localhost:8088). Blue regions mark phases; red markers are crashes and restarts."
   },
   "id": 1,
   "gridPos": {
    "x": 0,
    "y": 0,
    "w": 24,
    "h": 7
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "state-timeline",
   "title": "Phase",
   "datasource": {
    "type": "prometheus",
    "uid": "prometheus"
   },
   "targets": [
